{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/63775-solar-bureaucracy-help","id":63775,"title":"Solar Bureaucracy Help","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-02T22:33:27-08:00","id":63775,"title":"Solar Bureaucracy Help","content":"Our group is having a problem with the higher level Bureaucracy charms for 2.5.<br /> <br /> We are currently trying to organize trade for our &quot;small: kingdom with our neighbours. While we are succeeding using social combat to establish trade, we feel we are losing out with maximising our effectiveness with the Bureaucracy charms. Especially with Market Buster Strike, as we don't know how to use this beside making pig iron art worth resource 5 and guild supplied heroin resource 0.<br /> <br /> <br /> Could you please enlighten use on how you use Bureaucracy charms the Exalted way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1864-rkbinder","name":"rkbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T22:50:55-08:00","id":63784,"title":"","content":"Canon ones? I don't, really.<br /> <br /> In order to answer your question, I'm going to have to ask: does your party use the Creation-Ruling Mandate rules in Masters of Jade?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/673-requiem_jeer","name":"Requiem_Jeer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar673_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T23:29:45-08:00","id":63792,"title":"","content":"We don't. Forgot to look into that book.<br /> <br /> Is it worth it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1864-rkbinder","name":"rkbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T07:21:05-08:00","id":63959,"title":"","content":"Absolutely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T07:52:54-08:00","id":63981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rkbinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/63775-solar-bureaucracy-help?p=63792#post63792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We don't. Forgot to look into that book.<br /> <br /> Is it worth it?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a bit of a sub-game. But, for what it is, it's excellent.<br /> <br /> Market-Buster Strike? Cripple an economy. Remember the recession? That. Now, RP the consequences!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/921-malovich","name":"Malovich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar921_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T08:41:03-08:00","id":64024,"title":"","content":"It's also an absolutely beautiful book with loads of fun details.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T09:18:21-08:00","id":64054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rkbinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/63775-solar-bureaucracy-help#post63775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you please enlighten use on how you use Bureaucracy charms the Exalted way?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're automatically winning everything related to logistics or economy, as long as nothing equally powerful tries to hinder you. That includes Primordials, Solaroids, Incarnae and Pattern Spider (which are pretty pissed if you're using Market Buster Strike and similar things too often), but not much more.<br /> Solar Bureaucracy Charms should be used on a personal scope, not to print money for your group on a long-term base. Therefore you can just use Heaven-Ruling Mandate with no crossover-mechanics whatsoever. But that's not really roleplay, at least not on your characters' part.<br /> <br /> Btw, @Market-Buster Strike: It's not only possible to cripple an economy, you can also overload it for temporary messures. But in the end it's always bad for the economy you're tempering with. It's better to use it twice in a row, increasing the value while you're selling (or decreasing while buying) and resetting it in the next round. This minimizes the related damage. You could also try to control the market. That works to fight big corporations manipulating the prices themselves... probably only the Guild. After all, the entire charm does not create something from nothing, it decouples the price of an item from any questions of supply and demand (and it does it by using mindcontrol on every merchant/actor).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/239565-wizard-s-panoply-how-to-play-a-mage-in-exalted-collection-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Complete the Wizard's Panoply</a></b> [How to be a mage in Creation]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/442-nephtys","name":"Nephtys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar442_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}